    "_comment_gapfill": "Added 8 Aug from the unmapped tail. 4,843 rows had no shelf across 1,236 distinct supplier categories — a long tail, but the head of it is short: the top 150 categories carry two thirds of the rows. These are those, plus six new leaves for the things that genuinely had nowhere to go (DC jacks, hook-up wire, RFID, rules and tapes, coin cells, AC motors, robot wheels). Brand buckets are deliberately NOT here — \"Bosch Engineering Tools\" and \"DF Robot Modules\" hold unlike things, so one key would mis-file most of what it caught. `awg` was tried and dropped: it matches every wire gauge in every title, including cable already correctly shelved elsewhere."
  },
  "_comment_deferred": [
    "Product lines we are choosing not to list yet.",
    "",
    "These rows keep everything the crawl captured — price, stock, images, specs,",
    "datasheets — and are simply held out of the CSV, so switching one on later is",
    "an edit here rather than another pass over someone else's server.",
    "",
    "This exists because 'no category' and 'not yet' look identical once a row",
    "fails the importer, and six months from now nobody remembers which of the",
    "unmapped rows were a decision.",
    "",
    "To turn a line on: move its keys into categoryBySource pointing at real leaf",
    "paths, add the leaves to apps/web/src/lib/catalog.ts if they do not exist,",
    "then `node tools/feeds/pull.mjs --source=<name> --remap`. No re-crawl."
  ],
