  "_comment_weak": "Supplier categories that are a shelf rather than an answer, checked AFTER the title instead of before it. robu sweeps ~1,100 rows into \"<Brand> 3D Printer Parts\", which holds nozzles, hotends, belts, fans and sensors — things that live in four different L2 groups and two different L1 drawers. A weak key still catches whatever the title cannot name, so nothing loses its shelf; it just stops outranking a title that is more specific than it is. The test for adding one is not \"is this key vague\" but \"does this bucket mix unlike things\" — `relay` is broad and stays strong, because everything in it really is a relay. \"Other 3D Printer Accessories\" was in this list for one run and came straight back out: its rows are tape, MOSFETs and expansion modules whose titles all end \"for 3D Printers\", so weakening it handed 17 accessories to the `3d printer` title key and shelved them as machines. A catch-all whose fallback is already the right answer is not weak — it is just broad. \"FPV and Telemetry Transmitter-Receivers\" joined the list on the same test: 151 rows holding antennas, video transmitters, RC receivers, an ESC and a batch of LC power filters, of which about 15 were telemetry.",
  "_comment_projects": "Cross-build membership — the \"Used in these projects\" block. Keyed on a category PREFIX, longest wins, and deliberately sparse. The rule this respects is already written into skus.ts: derived-from-the-category-tree was tried and abandoned, because PROJECTS.spans lists \"Fasteners\" under Drone and that made every M3 screw in the catalogue claim it builds a drone. So the test here is not \"could this part appear in that build\" — nearly everything could — but \"is this part characteristic of it\": would a buyer seeing it on the build page think yes, obviously, rather than why. Whole drawers qualify where the drawer IS the build (drones-parts, ev-parts). Below that only a handful of L2 groups do. Everything unlisted stays empty, which is the correct and common answer, and a human can always add more on upload — the importer appends to builds.items and never removes.",
